Terminal 1: micro-ROS Agent (The Bridge)
(Make sure your PlatformIO Serial Monitor is CLOSED before running this!)
Bash

newgrp docker
docker run -it --rm --net=host --privileged -v /dev:/dev microros/micro-ros-agent:humble serial --dev /dev/ttyUSB0 -b 115200

    Action: Once you see running..., press the EN/RST button on your ESP32 board. Wait to see a message like "session established".

Terminal 2: Live Position Feed (The Monitor)
Run this to see the raw numbers directly from Motor 1.
Bash

source ~/Documents/PlatformIO/Projects/motor_pd_controller/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
ros2 topic echo /motor1/position

(Note: If you want to check the other motors, just change motor1 to motor2 or motor3 in the command).

Terminal 3: Build & Source (The Workspace)
(Only necessary if you edited your Python code)
Bash

cd ~/Documents/PlatformIO/Projects/motor_pd_controller/ros2_ws
colcon build --symlink-install
source install/setup.bash

Terminal 4: Launch Unified GUI (The Control Center)
Bash

source ~/Documents/PlatformIO/Projects/motor_pd_controller/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
ros2 run motor_controller pd_gui
